<!-- Like this title: an outline thumbs-up.

     The UNSIGNALLED state of the detail header's like toggle (see
     ic_detail_thumb_up_filled). Same 24x24 viewport, same box and baked
     kb_text_hi (#FFF3EFE4) as the filled mark - the difference is the open
     interior, so the button reads as one mark that fills once pressed.

     Path data is Google's Material Icons "thumb_up_off_alt" (24 unit viewport),
     copied rather than hand-drawn. The `_off_alt` variant is the one that
     publishes an OUTLINE of the thumb: the interior is cut out of the body
     (its own counter subpath) and the forearm, the knuckle and the cuff bar are
     all drawn as strokes of roughly one unit, which is what keeps the counter
     visibly open at the 18dp the header renders it at and the 22dp the phone
     does. The plain "thumb_up" path is solid, so it is the filled state's
     source, not this one's. -->
